# QuietVoice inferenced — AMD MI300X PREMIUM demo env (192 GB HBM3, gfx942 / CDNA3).
# `make mi300x` copies this to deploy/.env.mi300x if that file is missing, fetches the
# HF_MODELS below into MODELS_DIR, then `docker compose up`s the hot fleet:
#   3x qwen3-tts-1.7b-Q8 (say) + whisper-large-v3-turbo + voxtral-mini-4b (listen ensemble)
#   + 1x Gemma-4 12B bf16 (brain).
# Voxtral IS included: crispasr voxtral4b used to abort on gfx942 (HIP-graph capture bug), but
# GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1 (below) works around it — genuine Voxtral+Whisper ensemble on AMD
# (verified on real MI300X 2026-07-12: recovers "ChatGPT" + reads tone=annoyed vs whisper-only).
#
# ⚠️ DEMO token is intentionally DANGEROUS_CHANGE_ME. On a throwaway rented box that's an
# accepted risk (worst case = someone burns a one-time box's cycles; destroying the box wipes
# it). For anything you keep, set a real INFERENCE_TOKEN and reuse it in the Mac control plane.
# The /models/* paths MATCH the fetched filenames on purpose, so fetch → launch line up
# with no rename step. HF coords verified 2026-07-12 (all resolve 200).

INFERENCE_LISTEN=:9095
INFERENCE_ADMIN=1
INFERENCE_TOKEN=DANGEROUS_CHANGE_ME

# ⚠️ REQUIRED for Voxtral on gfx942: crispasr voxtral4b aborts on ROCm inside CUDA/HIP
# graph capture (get_rows k-quant calls hipStreamSynchronize mid-capture -> "operation not
# permitted when stream is capturing" -> Aborted/core dumped). Disabling ggml CUDA graphs
# avoids the illegal sync. Passed to all crispasr children; harmless (negligible perf) for
# whisper/TTS. Verified on real MI300X 2026-07-12.
GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1

# Prebuilt ROCm engine bundles (crispasr + llama.cpp) fetched at image-build time. compose
# reads these at interpolation time (via --env-file), so they MUST be set here. Build them
# from source on the MI300X box and upload to the release (see doc/rocm-mi300x-build.md).
CRISPASR_ROCM_URL=https://github.com/Ruslan/quietvoice/releases/download/engine-binaries-v1/rocm-mi300x-crispasr.tgz
LLAMACPP_ROCM_URL=https://github.com/Ruslan/quietvoice/releases/download/engine-binaries-v1/rocm-mi300x-llamacpp.tgz

# --- model fetch (make mi300x-models -> scripts/fetch-models.sh) ---
MODELS_DIR=/workspace/models
HF_MODELS="ggml-org/gemma-4-12B-it-GGUF::gemma-4-12B-it-bf16.gguf ggml-org/gemma-4-12B-it-GGUF::mmproj-gemma-4-12B-it-bf16.gguf ggerganov/whisper.cpp::ggml-large-v3-turbo.bin cstr/voxtral-mini-4b-realtime-GGUF::voxtral-mini-4b-realtime-q4_k.gguf cstr/qwen3-tts-1.7b-base-GGUF::qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b-base-q8_0.gguf cstr/qwen3-tts-tokenizer-12hz-GGUF::qwen3-tts-tokenizer-12hz.gguf"

# Rights-clean synthetic voice pack (10 voices, Qwen3-TTS VoiceDesign / Apache-2.0) —
# fetched + unpacked into VOICES_DIR (host), mounted into the container at TTS_VOICE_DIR.
VOICES_URL=https://github.com/Ruslan/quietvoice/releases/download/engine-binaries-v1/qwen-tts-synth-voices-v1.tgz
VOICES_DIR=/workspace/voices

# --- bundled ROCm binaries (baked into the image; see Dockerfile.inferenced-mi300x) ---
TTS_SERVER_BIN=/opt/qv/rocm-mi300x/crispasr
ASR_SERVER_BIN=/opt/qv/rocm-mi300x/crispasr
GEMMA_SERVER_BIN=/opt/qv/llamacpp/bin/llama-server
TTS_LIB_DIR=/opt/qv/rocm-mi300x/lib
GEMMA_LIB_DIR=/opt/qv/llamacpp/bin

# --- managed launch spec ---
TTS_VOICE_DIR=/voices
TTS_BASE_PORT=9100
TTS_MAX_REPLICAS=8

# TTS — qwen3-tts 1.7b Q8, 3 hot replicas
TTS_BACKEND=qwen3-tts
TTS_MODEL=/models/qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b-base-q8_0.gguf
TTS_CODEC_MODEL=/models/qwen3-tts-tokenizer-12hz.gguf
TTS_VOICE=voice01

# ASR — whisper large-v3-turbo (only recognizer; no voxtral on ROCm)
# TWO keys, TWO roles (don't drop WHISPER_MODEL):
#   ASR_MODEL    -> the hot asr replica pool + the raw /v1/audio/transcriptions path.
#   WHISPER_MODEL-> registers a "whisper-large" recognizer in the ENSEMBLE that
#                   literal/assisted use (engine.go builds Recognizers from
#                   VOXTRAL_MODEL/WHISPER_MODEL/ASR_RECOGNIZERS, NOT from ASR_MODEL).
# Without WHISPER_MODEL the ensemble is EMPTY, so assisted silently degrades to
# Gemma-audio-only (verified on real MI300X 2026-07-12 — no whisper anchor ran).
ASR_BACKEND=whisper
ASR_MODEL=/models/ggml-large-v3-turbo.bin
WHISPER_MODEL=/models/ggml-large-v3-turbo.bin
# VOXTRAL_MODEL registers the 2nd ensemble recognizer ("voxtral"). Boot a hot voxtral pool
# with N_VOXTRAL=1 below. Needs GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1 (above) on gfx942.
VOXTRAL_MODEL=/models/voxtral-mini-4b-realtime-q4_k.gguf
ASR_LANG=auto

# Gemma-4 12B bf16 — premium brain, interpret routes to this HOT llama-server
GEMMA_MODEL=/models/gemma-4-12B-it-bf16.gguf
GEMMA_MMPROJ=/models/mmproj-gemma-4-12B-it-bf16.gguf
# Gemma reasoning controls (big-VRAM node). The assisted ensemble with 2 ASR refs makes Gemma
# reason a LOT; unbounded it spirals to tens of thousands of reasoning tokens, hits the cap and
# returns EMPTY. Keep thinking but BOUND it so an answer is always emitted (verified MI300X
# 2026-07-12: budget 2048 -> ChatGPT recovered + tone=annoyed, 36 s). CTX is cheap at 192 GB.
GEMMA_CTX_SIZE=32768
GEMMA_MAX_TOKENS=4096
GEMMA_REASONING_BUDGET=2048

# --- boot-fabric.sh premium fleet (compose `boot` sidecar) ---
N_TTS=3
N_ASR=1
N_GEMMA=1
N_VOXTRAL=1
POLL_SECS=360

# --- optional: MIOpen tuning for gfx942 (only matters for long-form/book TTS) ---
# MIOPEN_FIND_MODE=NORMAL
# MIOPEN_USER_DB_PATH=/miopen-cache
